cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hydroweave in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Hydroweave: A Tibetan Plateau Cloud Water Resources Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Hydroweave is an experiment framework for Tibetan Plateau cloud water resources.
  It provides (1) proxy indicators computable from temperature and specific humidity
  alone (precipitable water, mid-level saturation, cloud-frequency proxy), (2) a complete
  water-substance budget model including gross cloud water retention (GCWR), precipitation
  efficiency and renewal periods, (3) a three-layer error analysis with first-order
  propagation and explicit falsifiability verdicts, and (4) a reproducibility contract
  with per-artifact SHA-256 fingerprints and independent adversarial acceptance.
  The proxy chain is validated on a real 2010-2013 ERA5 volume (736 warm-season days,
  10 hard acceptance criteria, single-column recomputation relative error 0.0000%);
  the budget model is regression-tested against published national-scale values.
